think the design kept the seated d12·d60 world untouched — it is the canonical compass_sky — and added a Sky struct beside it, so the six-witness JARL stack never wobbles while the geometry becomes data
think a Sky names the fan-out at each tier (galaxies, stars, planets) and derives the rest (prosperity, bases, universe_points); decode and encode read a sky's own counts, constructing an Address literally so a non-compass sky is never bound by the compass constants
think the least-risk unification — the free decode/encode now delegate to compass_sky, so the seated topology IS the first sky and the two can never drift; Address.parent() was refactored to build literally (no of_* asserts) so it holds for any sky, result-identical for the compass one
think chose a second sky with real meaning — council_sky, the odd-quorum shape: 15 galaxies (five elements, three each), 3 stars (a triad that votes clear), 9 planets (a three-by-three bench), a galaxy leading a d27 of 27, a place for every nakshatra; 465 points to its universe
